menu: the pre-filtered seeding keys two segments: true
menu: each segment offers three or more singles: true
off: no candidate carries a staff: true
off: the report counts no staffed window or fallback: true
on: the first key is swept bare (the composite starts empty): true
on: every single of the second key is staffed with the first key's fastest: true
on: every staffed window is counted: true
on: the crown is a staffed single holding each key's fastest: true
on: no bare retry without a refusal: true
on: the reference's singles, in the reference's order, only their backdrops differing: true
on: one window fewer than the reference, its coarse composite timed already: true
on: no composite window was timed: true
on and off: the same crown time: true
on: the best reaches the crown at the crown's own window: true
off: the best reaches the crown at the crown's own window: true
on: the crown's window is a single of the seed pass: true
off: the reference's crown is its coarse composite (the flat best this fixes): true
on: the crowned routine computes the untuned output bit for bit: true
replay: the staffed crown replays from the schedule cache: true
replay: the crown's schedule, at the time the search stored: true
replay: the replayed routine computes the untuned output bit for bit: true
start: the seam gave both keys a choice: true
start: the first key's own choice is swept first, staffed with the second's: true
start: every slower replacement left the first key's choice as it was: true
start: the second key's start choice, the timed composite by then, is not timed again: true
start: a faster single replaced the second key's start choice: true
start_refused: no refusal after the reused composite is retried bare: true
refused: one staffed single refused, one bare retry: true
refused: the attempt after the refusal is its bare twin: true
refused: the bare twin was timed: true
refused: the refused staffed single was never timed: true
refused: the refusal is a contained pre-dispatch decline: true
refused_all: every staffed refusal was retried bare, none of them admitted: true
progress: no attempt is counted past its phase's announced total: true
refused_after: after an admitted staffed single, no refusal of the key is retried bare: true
slower: the first key joined the composite: true
slower: no single of the slower key joined it: true
slower: the crown is the first key's single, the second on its preset: true
shrunk: three keys were swept: true
shrunk: the third key's bare single replaced the composite: true
shrunk: the report keeps the composite window it timed: true
refused_staffed: every refused staffed single was retried bare and timed: true
refused_staffed: the key's fastest bare retry, the faster routine, replaced the composite: true
refused_staffed: the crown is that bare single: true
partial: the cut search's report says the staffed composite was timed: true
ties: the playoff timed alternates: true
ties: every composite window is the playoff's: true
ties: only the first key plays; the last key's sweep ran inside the composite: true
ties finals: the same playoff alternates as with the finals off: true
ties finals: every alternate was decided by a finals, four windows each, all admitted: true
ties finals: the running composite was re-timed as an explicit composite, no alternate: true
ties finals: a tie keeps the running composite: true
heavy: the model weighs the second enumerated key the heavier: true
heavy: the keys are swept heaviest first: true
split: the first site is swept bare: true
split: every single of the second site is staffed with the first site's fastest: true
split: the composite was eligible and its window counted: true
split: no window re-timed the composite, the last accepted staffed single: true
split: the crown is a staffed single holding each site's fastest: true
split: the crowned routine computes the untuned output bit for bit: true
